<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the iPhone app.

  Required since 2024-05-01: App Store Connect refuses the UPLOAD, not merely
  the review, for an app that uses a required-reason API without declaring it.

  Every entry below is empty on purpose, and each emptiness is a fact that was
  checked rather than assumed:

  - No required-reason APIs. The phone app reads no file timestamps, no disk
    space, no active keyboard, and no system boot time. It also uses no
    UserDefaults: settings live in SettingsStore as JSON in Application Support,
    which is not a covered API.
  - No data collected. There is no analytics SDK, no crash reporter, no backend
    and no URLSession anywhere in the codebase. Nothing leaves the device.
  - No tracking, and no tracking domains.

  This stays accurate only while that remains true. Adding analytics, a food
  photo upload, RevenueCat, or a rest timer that reads systemUptime each means
  editing this file in the same commit. Verify with
  Product > Archive > Generate Privacy Report on the exact submission archive,
  and diff it against the App Store Connect privacy answers.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
